  "notes": [
   "The inventory pages were not included in the PDF provided, so no Element IDs could be read. Element IDs and colours were guessed from the catalogue (tan and dark red parts) by matching shapes in the pictures.",
   "Where the catalogue had no part in the right colour, I used a catalogue type and set the colour in props. Examples: the tan hinge plates use lego-4521427, and the tan horn cones use lego-4529236.",
   "The neck is a long dark-red piece with holes. I modelled it as lego-4495931 as a stand-in. It hinges to the body's front hinge plate (b7) and to the head's hinge plate (b12).",
   "Body steps 1-4 are only roughly resolved in the pictures. I assumed a 2x6 dark red base plate, tan and dark red bricks and plates stacked on it, and a dark red 1x4 plate on top. Exact sizes and positions are approximate.",
   "The two legs are built from the same sub-assembly (steps 5 and 6) and attach under the body base plate. The small differences in the leg stacks, for example 1x1 versus 1x2 bricks, were not resolved. They are modelled as two identical copies.",
   "Step 7 adds a dark red 1x4 plate (b8) with a tan hinge plate (b9). I placed it on top of the body plate b6 and treated it as the tail and back. The picture is ambiguous about which side the hinge points to.",
